sources.palette_lesson:
The source's specific scene colors are slate-navy walls, cream telescope paint, copper-gold emissive rims, white rays and one warm-orange UI accent. Treat these as one example for a night-sky subject, not as the defining palette. What carries over is the luminance structure:
- a low-key, desaturated environment;
- one neutral, matte hero material (here cream) so objects read as physical instruments;
- white or near-white additive lines for the thing being explained (light paths);
- a single warm saturated accent reserved for the selected or active state, with matching UI accents.

Keep the environment darker and cooler than the active accent, and keep caption text high-contrast against it.

